# Transient run artifacts -- regenerated locally, not version-controlled. Keep
# the folders (via .gitkeep) so a fresh clone has them ready, but ignore their
# (potentially large) contents.
state/*
cache/*
logs/*
!state/.gitkeep
!cache/.gitkeep
!logs/.gitkeep
.Renviron
.Rprofile
settings.local.R
# Working notes, not documentation: EM_COMBINE_COMPARISON.md compares this combiner against a
# sibling pipeline's. dev/README.md is deliberately TRACKED even though its Open threads
# section came from the untracked NEXT_STEPS.md -- a fresh clone with no orientation in dev/
# is how that file went stale unnoticed in the first place.
dev/EM_COMBINE_COMPARISON.md
nohup.out
# The container RECIPE is tracked, so `git pull` delivers it to any build host. The BUILT
# IMAGE never is: build.sh writes optimizer.sif into container/, and that is 1-2 GB of binary
# that would otherwise be swept up by `git add -A` on the build machine.
container/*.sif
# Per-machine submission settings (account, /project paths, node sizing). Same reason as
# settings.local.R above: the tracked t3opt_ceres.sh then stays identical everywhere and
# `git pull` never conflicts on it. Copy submit.local.sh.example to create it.
container/submit.local.sh
